# "You don't have to control either target" and "if the same player controls both creatures when Switcheroo resolves,
# nothing happens" (its rulings; CR 701.12b). Bot1 casts Switcheroo on two of Bot2's creatures, Llanowar Elves and
# Ornithopter: both stay Bot2's, and neither came under a new controller, so the Elves (cast on Bot2's turn before) taps
# for {G} on Bot2's next turn.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Sapphire
Mox Jet
Mox Ruby
Mox Pearl
Island
Switcheroo
Island x14

[Bot2 Deck]
Forest
Llanowar Elves
Ornithopter
Forest x17

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Island.Play
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot2.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Llanowar Elves.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Island.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Switcheroo.Cast
Bot1.Target(Bot2.Battlefield.Llanowar Elves; Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
[T4 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Battlefield.Llanowar Elves.Activate
? Bot2.Mana = {G}

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield = Mox Sapphire; Mox Jet; Mox Ruby; Mox Pearl; Island
Bot1.Graveyard = Switcheroo
Bot2.Battlefield = Forest; Llanowar Elves; Ornithopter
